    {
      "title": "IPOs lap up record ₹94,205 crore in April-September FY27: Report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/ipos-lap-up-record-94-205-crore-in-april-september-fy27-report-126100100972_1.html",
      "description": "Fund raising through initial public offers (IPOs) touched a record high of Rs 94,205 crore in April-September FY27, courtesy big-ticket issues such as by NSE, as per a report released by Primedatabase.com on Thursday.\nA total of 78 companies hit the market with main board IPOs in the six months totalling Rs 94,205 crore. The money raised is 35 per cent higher than the previous all-time high of Rs 69,533 crore mobilised by 65 IPOs in the same period last year, it said.\n\"This record fundraising has happened despite an extremely slow start to the year with only Rs 3,794 crore being raised in the first three months and also despite volatile secondary markets through most part of the six months,\"  company's managing director Pranav Haldea said.\nThe outlook for IPO activity is also bright, with a total of 145 candidates proposing to raise around Rs 2.78 lakh crore in the pipeline with Sebi approval, and another 102 companies entailing issuances of Rs 1.87 lakh crore awaiting the markets .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-01T13:23:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Net GST revenue rises 18.1% to ₹1.77 trn in September, fastest in 6 months",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/net-gst-revenue-rises-18-1-to-1-77-trn-in-september-fastest-in-6-months-126100100628_1.html",
      "description": "Gross GST collections rose 14.7 per cent to Rs 2.04 trillion, while net revenue growth accelerated to around 14 per cent in the July-September quarter",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-01T09:08:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Gross GST collections rise 14.7% to over ₹2.03 trillion in September",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/gross-gst-collections-rise-14-7-to-over-2-03-trillion-in-september-126100100388_1.html",
      "description": "Gross GST collections rose 14.7 per cent in September to over Rs 2.03 lakh crore.\nGross GST collections from domestic activities rose 10.1 per cent to about Rs 1.38 lakh crore, while revenues from imports were up 26 per cent to Rs 65,525 crore.\nGoods and Services Tax (GST) refunds, however, slowed to Rs 27,001 crore in September, a decline of 3 per cent year on year.\nAfter adjusting for refunds, net GST collections rose 18.1 per cent to over Rs 1.76 lakh crore in September.\nDuring the first half of the fiscal (April-September), gross GST collection grew 11.6 per cent to over Rs 12.46 lakh crore. Net collections rose 10.4 per cent to over Rs 10.66 lakh crore.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-01T06:32:14"
    }
  ]
